1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,640
You don't have to like me, okay?

2
00:00:06,180 --> 00:00:07,790
Huh?

3
00:00:07,790 --> 00:00:12,000
I was satisfied enough confessing to you.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,140
I won't ask for anything more.

5
00:00:15,430 --> 00:00:17,360
- But...
- Besides,

6
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:21,110
you're lovable to me

7
00:00:21,110 --> 00:00:24,570
like a local mascot would be.

8
00:00:24,570 --> 00:00:27,830
Nothing more than that.

9
00:00:27,830 --> 00:00:30,180
What the heck?

10
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:35,430
I was serious.

11
00:00:36,940 --> 00:00:41,390
<i>It was all a big misunderstanding?</i>

12
00:00:42,220 --> 00:00:46,400
Why didn't you tell me earlier?

13
00:00:51,160 --> 00:00:54,610
Now I've fallen for you for real.

14
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:04,000
Summer vacation offers many temptations.

15
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,990
But I want you all to be
model students of Kitahara.

16
00:01:07,990 --> 00:01:11,510
Remember, don't do anything crazy, okay?

17
00:01:11,510 --> 00:01:12,880
Yes, ma'am.

18
00:01:12,880 --> 00:01:15,710
Now go enjoy your break!

19
00:01:15,710 --> 00:01:20,800
Hell yeah!

20
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:24,180
Bye, teach!

21
00:01:34,860 --> 00:01:37,500
Let's go, let's go. Come on, baby.

22
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:42,570
Yeah, yeah, summer vacay!

23
00:01:44,470 --> 00:01:46,800
- Mayama.
- Huh?

24
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:49,020
Someone's not excited.

25
00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:52,020
Come on, it's summer break!

26
00:01:52,020 --> 00:01:55,910
Go, go, summer vacay!

27
00:01:55,910 --> 00:01:57,690
Tsunekawada and I were saying

28
00:01:57,690 --> 00:01:59,690
we should all take a trip together.

29
00:01:59,690 --> 00:02:02,900
My vote's in for the beach.

30
00:02:04,860 --> 00:02:06,130
Not an ocean guy?

31
00:02:06,130 --> 00:02:09,010
Then how about a mountain?
Or the opposite, a hot spring?

32
00:02:09,010 --> 00:02:10,480
How's that the opposite?

33
00:02:10,480 --> 00:02:12,390
Sorry.

34
00:02:12,390 --> 00:02:15,520
I'll be busy over break, with my...

35
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:19,680
my part-time job.

36
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:21,820
So, yeah.

37
00:02:21,820 --> 00:02:23,750
Hey!

38
00:02:27,660 --> 00:02:30,250
What's his deal?

39
00:02:30,250 --> 00:02:33,050
Guess it'll just be us three.

40
00:02:33,050 --> 00:02:35,310
Then how about the opposite
of hot springs, camping?

41
00:02:35,310 --> 00:02:38,040
You're losing me with these opposites, dude.

42
00:03:30,870 --> 00:03:34,650
<i>At first, I lied about the part-time job.</i>

43
00:03:34,650 --> 00:03:37,480
<i>But I realized it was actually a great idea.</i>

44
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,520
<i>I figured doing busy work</i>

45
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:45,810
<i>was a good way to forget Asamiya.</i>

46
00:03:46,680 --> 00:03:48,610
<i>Except...</i>

47
00:03:48,610 --> 00:03:51,860
This is no job to do in the summer.

48
00:03:55,250 --> 00:03:57,090
Okay, keep going.

49
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:05,060
Finally, I'm almost done...

50
00:04:14,050 --> 00:04:15,910
No flyers allowed.

51
00:04:15,910 --> 00:04:18,190
Sorry...

52
00:04:18,190 --> 00:04:19,790
Sakaki?

53
00:04:19,790 --> 00:04:22,530
Impressive vocal range, right?

54
00:04:22,530 --> 00:04:24,010
What are you doing here?

55
00:04:24,010 --> 00:04:28,400
I live here.

56
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:31,800
Oh, makes sense.

57
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:34,090
Sorry to bother.

58
00:04:34,090 --> 00:04:35,420
Where are you going?

59
00:04:35,420 --> 00:04:37,030
You said no flyers.

60
00:04:37,030 --> 00:04:38,870
I was joking.

61
00:04:38,870 --> 00:04:40,490
Leave all the flyers you want.

62
00:04:40,490 --> 00:04:42,480
Here, I'll help.

63
00:04:42,480 --> 00:04:43,980
Huh?

64
00:04:46,780 --> 00:04:48,760
How do I do this?

65
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:51,650
I've never left flyers before.

66
00:04:51,650 --> 00:04:53,160
Uh...

67
00:04:57,140 --> 00:04:59,380
Thanks, I appreciated the help.

68
00:04:59,380 --> 00:05:00,700
Anytime.

69
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:03,720
Didn't think you were
actually working though.

70
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:06,350
I thought that was just
an excuse to avoid us.

71
00:05:06,350 --> 00:05:09,280
Uh, well...

72
00:05:10,220 --> 00:05:12,450
Something on your mind?

73
00:05:13,650 --> 00:05:15,250
Huh?

74
00:05:15,250 --> 00:05:18,450
You've been down since the festival, right?

75
00:05:18,450 --> 00:05:20,760
Even I could tell.

76
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:25,330
If you'd rather not talk,
don't worry about it.

77
00:05:28,800 --> 00:05:33,340
You've had a couple of girlfriends, right?

78
00:05:33,340 --> 00:05:35,060
Yeah, unlike you.

79
00:05:35,060 --> 00:05:36,660
Hey.

80
00:05:38,280 --> 00:05:44,130
I was just wondering
what it meant to like someone.

81
00:05:45,270 --> 00:05:47,120
Thinking of becoming a poet?

82
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:50,220
I'm being serious here.

83
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:55,420
When I like someone, I want to be with them.

84
00:05:55,420 --> 00:05:58,980
I'd like to get touchy with them, too.

85
00:06:00,850 --> 00:06:02,780
But aren't there other types of "likes"?

86
00:06:02,780 --> 00:06:06,990
The non-romantic kind.

87
00:06:08,450 --> 00:06:10,190
Oh, the platonic sort of like?

88
00:06:10,190 --> 00:06:11,590
Yeah.

89
00:06:11,590 --> 00:06:13,660
Okay, I understand your conundrum now.

90
00:06:13,660 --> 00:06:18,750
I think your lack of romantic experience
is to blame, though.

91
00:06:18,750 --> 00:06:21,320
Can't deny that.

92
00:06:21,320 --> 00:06:24,490
You need to live a little, Mayama.

93
00:06:24,490 --> 00:06:26,700
It works out, since I'm single, too.

94
00:06:28,390 --> 00:06:31,970
Why is your relationship status
relevant to our conversation?

95
00:06:31,970 --> 00:06:34,000
It's super relevant.

96
00:06:34,870 --> 00:06:36,460
They have room for one more.

97
00:06:36,460 --> 00:06:38,070
You're done with work for the day, right?

98
00:06:38,070 --> 00:06:41,520
- Yeah.
- Then let's go.

99
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:44,310
Huh?

100
00:06:44,310 --> 00:06:45,790
Hey, wait!

101
00:06:47,300 --> 00:06:48,640
Where are we going?

102
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:50,350
- Karaoke.
- Huh?

103
00:06:50,350 --> 00:06:53,620
But this is no ordinary karaoke outing.

104
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:55,820
- Sakaki.
- 'Sup man!

105
00:06:56,480 --> 00:06:58,830
- So...
- We're joining a mixer.

106
00:06:58,830 --> 00:07:01,230
What? I didn't sign up for this.

107
00:07:01,230 --> 00:07:02,480
You wanted to know a girl's heart.

108
00:07:02,480 --> 00:07:05,110
I never said that!

109
00:07:05,110 --> 00:07:06,360
- Just trust me.
- But...

110
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:08,900
Huh? Sakaki and Mayama.

111
00:07:10,090 --> 00:07:12,020
Asamiya...

112
00:07:12,020 --> 00:07:15,000
- What're you two up to?
- Shopping. You two?

113
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:17,160
- Can't you tell?
- Hey!

114
00:07:17,160 --> 00:07:20,510
- We're getting ready for a mixer.
- You and your mixers, Sakaki.

115
00:07:20,510 --> 00:07:22,350
- Is Mayama joining you?
- No, I...

116
00:07:22,350 --> 00:07:27,260
Yeah. He begged me to join.

117
00:07:27,260 --> 00:07:28,350
Let's leave them.

118
00:07:28,350 --> 00:07:30,430
- Sure.
- See you two.

119
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:34,790
Go on.

120
00:07:34,790 --> 00:07:37,290
Head on in.

121
00:07:39,270 --> 00:07:41,920
What're you doing? Come on.

122
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:47,300
♪ <i>La La Love You A to Z,
I'll never know it's not mutual</i> ♪

123
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:52,220
♪ <i>La La Love you A to Z</i> ♪

124
00:07:52,220 --> 00:07:54,890
Thank you very much!

125
00:07:54,890 --> 00:07:56,490
Let's get hyped up!

126
00:07:56,490 --> 00:07:58,280
- Yeah!
- Great opener!

127
00:07:58,280 --> 00:08:00,490
You're a good singer.

128
00:08:00,490 --> 00:08:03,440
Here, sing a song and introduce yourself.

129
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:06,030
Huh? Oh, uh...

130
00:08:07,230 --> 00:08:08,670
Here.

131
00:08:21,110 --> 00:08:23,110
I'm Mayama.

132
00:08:25,340 --> 00:08:29,540
That's all. I'll sing later.

133
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:34,680
Yeah, give it up!

134
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:36,500
All right, who's next?

135
00:08:37,210 --> 00:08:42,130
<i>Asamiya definitely misunderstood.</i>

136
00:08:42,130 --> 00:08:43,810
I'll sort through all this...

137
00:08:43,810 --> 00:08:45,970
Your iced coffees. Enjoy.

138
00:08:46,980 --> 00:08:49,780
That was a real shocker, huh?

139
00:08:49,780 --> 00:08:52,570
I didn't think Mayama went to mixers.

140
00:08:54,690 --> 00:08:57,840
Sorry to call on you like this.

141
00:08:57,840 --> 00:08:59,310
You definitely surprised me.

142
00:08:59,310 --> 00:09:03,360
I never thought you'd come to me for advice.

143
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:05,500
So, what's up?

144
00:09:08,680 --> 00:09:10,890
I have a crush on someone.

145
00:09:12,940 --> 00:09:15,010
Yeah.

146
00:09:15,010 --> 00:09:16,820
You're not surprised?

147
00:09:18,950 --> 00:09:20,600
No, I am.

148
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:24,350
I've never heard you mention a crush.

149
00:09:25,420 --> 00:09:28,410
So, what are they like?

150
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:32,700
They're kind.

151
00:09:33,540 --> 00:09:39,660
They prioritize others over themself.

152
00:09:41,730 --> 00:09:45,880
Before I knew it, I liked them.

153
00:09:46,780 --> 00:09:49,360
And I told them how I felt, too.

154
00:09:50,330 --> 00:09:51,700
But...

155
00:09:51,700 --> 00:09:55,480
The other party turned you down?

156
00:09:57,520 --> 00:10:02,460
No. I told them they didn't need to like me.

157
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:05,270
Why?

158
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:09,370
Because they're so kind.

159
00:10:11,710 --> 00:10:13,900
Because they're too kind.

160
00:10:14,520 --> 00:10:18,880
I can tell he's desperate

161
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:21,130
<i>to live up to everyone's expectations.</i>

162
00:10:21,130 --> 00:10:23,100
I didn't want them

163
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:26,510
to feel forced to like me.

164
00:10:27,410 --> 00:10:29,580
I was worried they would be considerate,

165
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:36,010
and try to like me out of pity.

166
00:10:36,010 --> 00:10:38,520
And that won't do for you.

167
00:10:39,550 --> 00:10:43,870
Yeah. What I want isn't something like that.

168
00:10:45,840 --> 00:10:47,820
- Woah.
- You play guitar?

169
00:10:47,820 --> 00:10:52,770
<i>I'd be happy if they earnestly fell for me.</i>

170
00:10:52,770 --> 00:10:55,080
<i>But if that weren't the case...</i>

171
00:10:56,270 --> 00:10:58,090
It wouldn't be...

172
00:11:00,980 --> 00:11:04,030
what I wanted from them.

173
00:11:05,230 --> 00:11:06,870
So...

174
00:11:08,930 --> 00:11:11,910
Your romance is a difficult one, huh?

175
00:11:17,380 --> 00:11:18,700
What?

176
00:11:18,700 --> 00:11:23,900
Nothing. I'm just surprised to see
a guy like you worry, too.

177
00:11:23,900 --> 00:11:25,780
I'm not joking around.

178
00:11:25,780 --> 00:11:27,040
Sorry.

179
00:11:27,040 --> 00:11:32,750
If anything, I'm embarrassed.
I've never opened up like this before.

180
00:11:32,750 --> 00:11:36,250
Well, I'm happy to see you fumbling about.

181
00:11:36,250 --> 00:11:37,330
Huh?

182
00:11:37,330 --> 00:11:41,400
Why don't you open up to them like this?

183
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:46,460
Tell them you're feeling confused,
and tangled up inside.

184
00:11:46,460 --> 00:11:49,720
I'm sure they'll understand.

185
00:11:54,720 --> 00:12:00,110
Or do you not trust
the person you're crushing on?

186
00:12:01,420 --> 00:12:02,970
No, I do.

187
00:12:05,650 --> 00:12:07,900
I'd love to meet them one day.

188
00:12:07,900 --> 00:12:11,830
Since you're so obsessed with them and all.

189
00:12:23,280 --> 00:12:25,130
Mayama?

190
00:12:54,900 --> 00:12:58,120
I'll be rooting for you.

191
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:16,170
♪ <i>All night, all night, all night, you</i> ♪

192
00:13:16,170 --> 00:13:18,140
You're good!

193
00:13:18,140 --> 00:13:20,210
A natural!

194
00:13:20,210 --> 00:13:22,770
Great job!

195
00:13:22,770 --> 00:13:25,340
Why did I pick a song in English?

196
00:13:25,340 --> 00:13:28,280
I'm going to the restroom.

197
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:29,960
Your pronunciation was good!

198
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:31,980
The restroom...

199
00:13:31,980 --> 00:13:33,420
I thought you were a native!

200
00:13:33,420 --> 00:13:36,060
You're making fun of me.

201
00:13:36,060 --> 00:13:39,200
[Karaoke Entertainment BIG ECHO]

202
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:43,380
- You know, Sakaki's friend we saw earlier.
- Yeah?

203
00:13:43,380 --> 00:13:45,930
Asamiya, I think. He was so good-looking.

204
00:13:45,930 --> 00:13:49,670
He was so high caliber, I'm falling for him.

205
00:13:49,670 --> 00:13:51,170
You have a boyfriend!

206
00:13:51,170 --> 00:13:53,370
I like him for a different reason.

207
00:13:53,370 --> 00:13:55,940
Why are you at this mixer anyway?

208
00:13:55,940 --> 00:14:01,220
<i>Right. Of course Asamiya
wouldn't really like me.</i>

209
00:14:01,220 --> 00:14:03,660
<i>It's just not possible.</i>

210
00:14:03,660 --> 00:14:05,150
I didn't tell him I'd be here.

211
00:14:05,150 --> 00:14:07,430
Then are you aiming for someone?

212
00:14:07,430 --> 00:14:09,440
Hey.

213
00:14:09,440 --> 00:14:11,340
What are you doing?

214
00:14:11,340 --> 00:14:13,590
I came looking for you.

215
00:14:13,590 --> 00:14:15,130
For me?

216
00:14:15,130 --> 00:14:17,620
And now that I've found you,

217
00:14:17,620 --> 00:14:20,380
I've decided to watch you freeze in place.

218
00:14:23,910 --> 00:14:25,530
Wait.

219
00:14:28,300 --> 00:14:30,260
Go home.

220
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:37,440
You're the one who drew the line first.

221
00:14:42,080 --> 00:14:45,360
Encore, encore!

222
00:14:45,360 --> 00:14:48,050
Welcome back.

223
00:14:48,050 --> 00:14:49,480
Here.

224
00:14:49,480 --> 00:14:51,920
Sing us a song.

225
00:14:53,870 --> 00:14:56,570
- He's singing?
- Finally!

226
00:14:56,570 --> 00:14:58,100
What're you gonna sing?

227
00:14:58,100 --> 00:15:01,670
- An English song?
- Seriously, stop that!

228
00:15:04,630 --> 00:15:05,840
Asamiya?

229
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:08,100
The good-looking guy from earlier!

230
00:15:09,060 --> 00:15:10,660
We're leaving.

231
00:15:13,620 --> 00:15:15,380
Where are they going?

232
00:15:15,380 --> 00:15:17,640
Home, I guess.

233
00:15:23,350 --> 00:15:26,600
Did you enjoy the mixer?

234
00:15:26,600 --> 00:15:29,380
I was dragged into it.

235
00:15:30,650 --> 00:15:33,090
I'm jealous of Sakaki.

236
00:15:33,090 --> 00:15:35,850
He gets to be all touchy with you.

237
00:15:46,250 --> 00:15:47,670
Huh?

238
00:15:50,720 --> 00:15:55,310
Did you do this sort of thing with him?

239
00:15:55,310 --> 00:15:57,550
Of course not.

240
00:16:04,540 --> 00:16:06,700
And this?

241
00:16:12,050 --> 00:16:15,810
How does this make you feel?

242
00:16:17,890 --> 00:16:20,200
I don't know.

243
00:16:21,240 --> 00:16:23,900
It's all a first for me.

244
00:16:28,420 --> 00:16:30,600
Your face is red.

245
00:16:39,020 --> 00:16:44,320
I haven't been able to see you
since summer vacation began.

246
00:16:45,530 --> 00:16:47,860
It's been bothering me a lot.

247
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:54,780
I wanted you to be around more.

248
00:16:59,590 --> 00:17:01,840
You're playing dirty.

249
00:17:04,240 --> 00:17:08,620
How are you expecting me to respond?

250
00:17:08,620 --> 00:17:11,810
I don't get you, Asamiya.

251
00:17:15,910 --> 00:17:18,670
You're the one who drew the line.

252
00:17:20,110 --> 00:17:22,930
Don't jump over it again.

253
00:17:24,560 --> 00:17:26,170
Sorry.

254
00:17:28,580 --> 00:17:30,370
I...

255
00:17:32,430 --> 00:17:37,600
I was seriously thinking about you.

256
00:17:40,860 --> 00:17:44,830
I know you'd never get it,
since you're so perfect, but...

257
00:17:49,600 --> 00:17:51,930
I'm not perfect.

258
00:17:54,220 --> 00:17:55,680
Huh?

259
00:17:58,400 --> 00:18:01,040
You overheard those girls, right?

260
00:18:02,510 --> 00:18:04,300
All my life,

261
00:18:05,210 --> 00:18:08,530
I've been judged for my looks.

262
00:18:09,900 --> 00:18:12,300
Everyone expects the best from me.

263
00:18:12,300 --> 00:18:15,200
When I fail, they say I'm just a face.

264
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:17,640
They're all quick to be disappointed.

265
00:18:22,010 --> 00:18:25,200
I'm constantly struggling to stay afloat.

266
00:18:27,470 --> 00:18:29,930
Honestly, I'm a wreck right now.

267
00:18:31,670 --> 00:18:34,430
My feelings are already out of whack

268
00:18:34,430 --> 00:18:37,000
because you're sitting next to me.

269
00:18:38,170 --> 00:18:41,220
I don't want to hurt you.

270
00:18:42,120 --> 00:18:44,600
I want to clear up the misunderstanding.

271
00:18:45,860 --> 00:18:48,180
It's all a tangled mess in my head.

272
00:18:50,850 --> 00:18:53,470
But...

273
00:18:53,470 --> 00:18:56,340
I want to seem composed in front of you.

274
00:18:58,350 --> 00:19:01,210
I want to look calm and cool.

275
00:19:04,910 --> 00:19:08,150
What misunderstanding?

276
00:19:13,290 --> 00:19:16,890
You're not a mascot.

277
00:19:21,890 --> 00:19:26,180
I didn't want you to "like" me out of pity,

278
00:19:26,180 --> 00:19:30,560
and not actually feel that way.

279
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:32,580
That's why I made that excuse.

280
00:19:33,380 --> 00:19:35,630
What?

281
00:19:35,630 --> 00:19:37,190
But...

282
00:19:38,300 --> 00:19:41,140
I went about it the wrong way.

283
00:19:41,140 --> 00:19:42,730
I'm sorry.

284
00:19:47,370 --> 00:19:48,920
Then...

285
00:19:50,570 --> 00:19:55,830
Whenever you said you liked me...

286
00:19:55,830 --> 00:19:58,390
You didn't mean it platonically?

287
00:20:01,170 --> 00:20:03,420
I obviously meant it romantically.

288
00:20:07,610 --> 00:20:10,260
I want to hold hands with you.

289
00:20:10,260 --> 00:20:13,130
I want to hug you tight.

290
00:20:13,130 --> 00:20:14,910
And...

291
00:20:17,830 --> 00:20:20,530
I want to be with you whenever I can.

292
00:20:31,270 --> 00:20:32,970
Mayama?

293
00:20:36,650 --> 00:20:39,540
What a relief.

294
00:20:43,400 --> 00:20:46,410
I thought I had no chance.

295
00:20:48,170 --> 00:20:49,180
Sorry.

296
00:20:49,180 --> 00:20:52,280
Liking you, "out of pity"?

297
00:20:53,330 --> 00:20:55,580
I wouldn't do that.

298
00:20:57,330 --> 00:21:00,020
So, don't draw a line between us anymore.

299
00:21:02,350 --> 00:21:03,870
I won't.

300
00:21:07,310 --> 00:21:10,190
Asamiya.

301
00:21:10,190 --> 00:21:12,200
I like you, okay?

302
00:21:16,800 --> 00:21:19,060
In what way?

303
00:21:20,220 --> 00:21:21,730
Huh?

304
00:21:23,380 --> 00:21:26,960
I told you exactly what I meant.

305
00:21:27,810 --> 00:21:31,740
So, tell me.

306
00:21:32,450 --> 00:21:37,520
What do you mean when you "like" me?

307
00:21:45,480 --> 00:21:49,990
I want to touch you.

308
00:21:55,630 --> 00:21:59,860
I also want to hold hands with you.

309
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:02,950
I want to hug you tight, too.

310
00:22:02,950 --> 00:22:05,130
That's what my "like" means.

311
00:22:14,710 --> 00:22:16,350
Sorry.

312
00:22:19,550 --> 00:22:21,230
It's fine.

313
00:22:24,100 --> 00:22:26,400
I liked that.

314
00:22:33,180 --> 00:22:35,010
Your phone's buzzing.

315
00:23:12,810 --> 00:23:15,250
See you soon...

316
00:23:15,940 --> 00:23:17,670
Kou.

317
00:24:41,310 --> 00:24:42,680
I'm the boyfriend.

318
00:24:42,680 --> 00:24:44,050
I know.

319
00:24:44,050 --> 00:24:45,630
Want to go together?

320
00:24:45,630 --> 00:24:47,610
Let's make real summer memories.

321
00:24:47,610 --> 00:24:50,380
I didn't think it'd be a gig at the festival.

322
00:24:50,380 --> 00:24:52,100
Kou!

323
00:24:52,100 --> 00:24:56,100
Who is she to Asamiya?

